## LC closing register · `sec:nrz:lc-closing-register`

**Convention (Closing claims and measured standing)** · `conv:nrz:lc-closing-standing`

Each claim below names a closing obligation and cites its governing contract; each group table cites those claims without declaring new ones. Met means the stated scope has executable cited evidence, partial means a tested subset leaves the named integration open, open means no closing executable evidence is identified, and follow-on means the capability is outside LC closing by its claim. A design statement or reference answer alone never establishes an implemented publication. Follow-on capabilities are explicitly marked in their claims and do not block LC closing. The boundary claims delimit the target rather than add implementations to it. The register is the completion authority for (`dec:nrz:lc-resonance-delivery-contract`); a supported component in (`tab:nrz:lc-resonance-capability-routes`) does not close the whole target.

**Observation (Closing evidence source baseline)** · `obs:nrz:lc-closing-baseline`

The inspected source is `b0de8e9e845c172e20dd611bbcb1055ce1c5454c`. Every existing closing claim has been re-inspected against its source and executable assertions; the tables cite test labels for implemented scope and name the evidence still missing. These statuses record source inspection, not a new test run or performance measurement. The numerical and allocation audits retain their measured scopes (`sec:nrz:matrix-acceptance-lc`), (`sec:nrz:matrix-native-phasor-inventory`), (`obs:nrz:computation-lc-plan-baseline`). The per-cell measurements remain those of (`sec:nrz:lc-grid-standing`): exact work is rebuilt for each answer, generic nonsquare products are refused by the forward adapter, and the largest certified population is 10⁵ cells; billion-cell costs are projections. Masked kernels, chained applications, prepared owners and host sampling are prerequisites, not tiled LC or stream acceptance.

**Rule (Every closing claim must be met)** · `rule:nrz:lc-closing-completion`

The LC target is closed only when every closing claim in this register is met and the independent candidate-main review reports `LC DONE` under (`rule:nrz:lc-closing-independent-review`); follow-on claims and explicit model exclusions are not closing implementations. At (`obs:nrz:lc-closing-baseline`) LC is not closed. Physical/plan integration, relation coverage and live refinement, engine tile/lambda/cache/walk integration, generic nonsquare LC lowering, tiled answers and decisions, standing streams and drain, complete cost attribution, fresh-process evidence, actual billion-cell scale and the explained certification-overhead model, budget, tracking and bound remain open or partial. No independent whole-repository closing verdict is established by this inspection. The count of met component rows is not a measure of proximity to completion. (`sec:nrz:backlog-lc-closing`) orders the remaining work without supplying a second completion authority.

**Rule (Independent whole-repository closing verdict)** · `rule:nrz:lc-closing-independent-review`

After every closing claim is met, LC closing requires an independent review on a model other than the producers' of the whole repository at the candidate main. The review reads the closing register, backlog, plan, LC designs and the code and tests they cite, checks their agreement and the evidence for every closing claim, and records the candidate commit and an explicit `LC DONE` verdict. It must verify the theoretical model, predicted overhead budget, measured component tracking and measured bound (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-naive-model`), (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-overhead-budget`), (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-overhead-tracking`), (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-overhead-bound`), including the actual billion-cell run. The alternative verdict is a list of blocking findings, each citing the labels it concerns. Each finding becomes or updates a labelled backlog item, with affected claim standing kept consistent; a blocking finding prevents closure until addressed and independently reviewed. A producer's completion claim, a green documentation check or a review of a smaller component cannot supply this verdict.

### Physical answers · `sec:nrz:lc-closing-physical-answers`

**Claim (Published natural angular frequency)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-angular-frequency`

LC closing requires a tested published angular-frequency value under (`rule:nrz:lc-angular-frequency-output`), (`rule:nrz:lc-angular-frequency-publication`), including the reference in (`tab:nrz:lc-resonance-answers`). This is a primary physical result with live value, error and source-model obligations, so a corpus coordinate cannot close it. The evidence is composite through the shared spectral producer: (`[MATRIX-test:integration:lc-spectral-published-reference-pair]`) checks the nominal positive rate of 2000 per second in binary64, which the sealed one-radian relation interprets as 2000 rad/s; (`[MATRIX-test:integration:lc-angular-frequency-original-center-output]`) checks original-center sensitivity and variance in both formats, and (`[MATRIX-test:integration:lc-angular-frequency-atomic-publication-boundaries]`) checks atomic angular publication and heap-value equality in both formats. The connected publisher retains that same producer and angular packing: (`[MATRIX-test:integration:lc-frequency-connected-original-output]`) checks the original model and connected bundle, (`[MATRIX-test:integration:lc-frequency-reference-and-period-oracle]`) checks the nominal cyclic reference and inverse period in both formats, and (`[MATRIX-test:integration:lc-frequency-deterministic-numerical-channels]`) checks equality of the angular value and deterministic channels with the retained spectral rate in both formats. These jointly support the stated value, publication and source-model scope; they are not a standalone both-format nominal angular-publisher oracle. The separate quantity chain retains its own operating-point policy.

**Claim (Published cyclic frequency)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-cyclic-frequency`

LC closing requires the tested connected frequency publication of (`rule:nrz:lc-cyclic-frequency-output`), (`rule:nrz:lc-frequency-bundle-boundary`), because the distinct kind and full-cycle relation must survive numerical publication. The exact nominal `1000/pi Hz` in (`tab:nrz:lc-resonance-answers`) is an independent oracle, not the algorithm or a substitute for the published pair.

**Claim (Reference period and its inverse check)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-period`

The reference period in (`tab:nrz:lc-resonance-answers`), with the independent enclosure of (`arg:nrz:lc-resonance-irrational-enclosures`), closes the period answer when an executable inverse check agrees with published cyclic frequency. Period adds no independent physical degree of freedom to that full-cycle result; a separate period publisher is not a closing prerequisite. This exception does not turn a caller-declared period into an LC-derived frequency (`rule:nrz:lc-resonance-kinds`).

**Claim (Reference characteristic impedance)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-characteristic-impedance`

The reference characteristic impedance in (`tab:nrz:lc-resonance-answers`) requires a checked value and a queryable amplitude ratio under (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-any-direction`), with no additional dedicated heap publisher. The reference spectral test checks 50 ohms, and the relation projection queries the ratio from supplied capacitance and voltage against independent rational endpoint oracles in both formats (`[MATRIX-test:integration:lc-spectral-published-reference-pair]`), (`[MATRIX-test:integration:lc-relation-query-ratio-energy]`). This meets the value-and-query scope of this claim. General combinations of supplied and queried quantities remain under (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-relation-quantities`); this result does not close that broader interface.

**Claim (Published complete state spectrum)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-state-eigenvalues`

LC closing requires the tested complete conjugate publication of (`step:nrz:lc-resonance-spectral-lowering`), including all component readings and the rates in (`tab:nrz:lc-resonance-answers`). Completeness, rate kind and shared-view lifetime are physical obligations that corpus coordinates alone cannot establish; the retained-evaluation publisher preserves the original producer under (`[MATRIX-rule:matrix:lc-retained-spectrum-publication]`).

**Claim (Published initial energy from the original state)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-initial-energy`

LC closing requires a tested published source-free energy from the original L/C and restored state, under (`step:nrz:lc-resonance-coordinate-lowering`), with independent nominal `1/8000 J` and varied-box oracles from (`tab:nrz:lc-resonance-answers`). Energy exercises state restoration and source dependencies that frequency does not, so the corpus answer alone is insufficient. The existing native recipe checks `37/128 J` and all original box corners in binary64; the nominal reference and both-format closing coverage remain to be joined to the plan. Energy is also supplied and queried on the restricted pair relation (`[MATRIX-test:integration:lc-relation-amplitude-energy]`), (`[MATRIX-test:integration:lc-relation-query-ratio-energy]`); that evidence does not replace original-state publication or close the general interface (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-relation-quantities`).

**Claim (Published driven series impedance rows)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-driven-impedance`

LC closing requires tested publications of all three original-expression impedance rows under (`rule:nrz:lc-plan-schedule`), (`req:nrz:lc-plan-completion-evidence`). The values in (`tab:nrz:lc-resonance-answers`) are independent targets; imported fixed impedance blocks and checked sign consumers do not prove that a plan computed them from L, C and each frequency. Exact zero must remain a successful impedance value. The explicit deterministic-point producer now computes the written expression after the retained invariant (`obs:nrz:lc-plan-impedance-production`); automatic composition into the complete driven owner and shared-voltage experiment remains required.

**Claim (Published nonzero phase branches)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-driven-phase`

LC closing requires tested angle-difference value publication below and above resonance, preserving (`rule:nrz:lc-sign-axis-quantity-boundary`) and the complete output slots of (`rule:nrz:lc-plan-schedule`). The corpus phases in (`tab:nrz:lc-resonance-answers`) close only their independent derivation. The tested live axis attachment returns certified phase enclosures, but no heap phase-value binding, so its guard authority is partial publication evidence.

**Claim (Undefined phase and the admittance pole)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-resonant-domains`

LC closing requires executable undefined-phase and unavailable current/admittance outcomes at proved resonance under (`rule:nrz:lc-resonance-phasor-domains`), (`rule:nrz:lc-plan-schedule`). These are domain answers, not finite values to publish: the corpus pole and undefined phase in (`tab:nrz:lc-resonance-answers`) must be backed by tested refusal and explicit absence. Preserve independent zero impedance, spectrum and frequency; unavailable current is never a zero current or a zero covariance block.

