### Reproducibility and registration · `sec:nrz:lc-closing-reproducibility`

**Claim (Fresh-process agreement and provenance)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-reproducibility`

LC closing requires (`req:nrz:lc-resonance-replay-verification`), delivered by (`step:nrz:lc-resonance-record-bite`): fresh-process agreement within tracked error with original inputs, semantic outcomes and admitted build/arithmetic provenance. Same-process tests, portable symbolic replay and unchanged output bits do not discharge that numerical requirement.

**Requirement (Integrated LC evidence register)** · `req:nrz:lc-integrated-evidence-register`

The reproducibility step shall assemble the closing claims, actual executable test labels, admitted instances/formats, original input and assumption identities, published value/error/domain outcomes, dependency mutations, owner overlap map and whole-attempt resource evidence in one inspectable record. Preserve the distinction between reference derivation, component acceptance and complete plan acceptance, and include fresh-process provenance and any unresolved outcomes. This is an evidence obligation under (`step:nrz:lc-resonance-record-bite`), not a new wire format or a claim that this design table executes the plan.

**Claim (Integrated evidence accompanies closing)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-integrated-evidence`

LC closing requires (`req:nrz:lc-integrated-evidence-register`). The scoped audits cited by (`obs:nrz:lc-closing-baseline`) remain reusable inputs, but cannot replace the missing integrated execution and reproducibility record.

**Claim (Registration optimization is optional)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-registration-optimization`

LC closing does not require the optional optimization in (`req:nrz:quantity-graph-registration-reuse`), (`dec:nrz:quantity-registration-owner`). Frozen environments and shared header segments already have evidence under (`ex:nrz:quantity-registration-key-segment-result`); additional reuse must justify its measured benefit and preserve (`rule:nrz:quantity-registration-freshness`), (`rule:nrz:quantity-registration-accounting`). This optional registration optimization is not itself a closing prerequisite; the complete LC path must still meet the separate explained-overhead claims (`sec:nrz:lc-closing-certification-cost`) under (`dec:nrz:lc-resonance-delivery-contract`).

**Requirement (Standalone registration design boundary)** · `req:nrz:lc-standalone-registration-design`

A standalone registration proposal shall specify a bindings-owned immutable checked definition/instantiation authority that can prepare fresh symbols without running an LC numerical operation. Reuse requires the original frozen declaration owner/revision, descriptors, ordered relations and policy; it grants no heap value or numerical validity. Define preparation, atomic commit, rollback, owner disposal and stale-generation refusal, with separate cold/warm Work and storage evidence and fresh value/companion identities. The enclosing operation must retain its existing publication transaction. This separates registration from evaluation without duplicating CAS authority or changing a wire format, under (`dec:nrz:quantity-registration-owner`), (`rule:nrz:quantity-registration-freshness`), (`rule:nrz:quantity-registration-accounting`), (`req:nrz:quantity-registration-boundaries`).

