### Relation quantities · `sec:nrz:lc-closing-relation`

**Claim (Every relation quantity can be supplied or queried)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-relation-quantities`

LC closing requires the common relation of (`def:nrz:lc-relation`), its quantity meanings (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-kinds`) and its any-direction interface (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-any-direction`). Reference answers and individual forward publishers do not establish this inverse/consistency interface; the characteristic ratio and energy are queryable quantities even when no separate dedicated heap publisher is needed.

**Claim (Certified sets retain all cycle branches)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-relation-sets`

LC closing requires the certified set coverage, explicit input ranges and complete extra-cycle inventory of (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-certified-sets`), (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-cycle-branches`). A single nominal solution, statistical confidence region or silently bounded alias search cannot close this claim.

**Claim (Determinacy and certainty are independent verdicts)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-relation-verdicts`

LC closing requires both verdicts of (`def:nrz:lc-relation-determinacy`), (`def:nrz:lc-relation-certainty`), with the same-question evidence boundary in (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-decision-correspondence`). In particular, certified underdetermination and numerically undecided determination must both be representable; impossibility needs complete certified emptiness.

**Claim (Time queries retain numbering and a justified tail)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-inverse-time`

LC closing requires the inverse query of (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-time-queries`), including ordered numbered boxes and the proved overlap tail of (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-overlap-tail`). Finite materialization must not truncate an infinite answer or invent a bound when a finite tail cannot be certified.

**Claim (Forward certainty horizon is a published value)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-certainty-horizon`

LC closing requires a published horizon with its own derivation and enclosure under (`rule:nrz:lc-relation-forward-horizon`). An infinite horizon or an undecided horizon remains explicit; a caller must not infer it from a truncated list of time boxes.

**Claim (Refinement preserves information)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-relation-monotonicity`

LC closing requires property evidence for (`req:nrz:lc-relation-refinement-monotonicity`): added pairs or tighter declared enclosures shrink the retained answer set and do not move a certified certainty horizon earlier or discard already proved information. Changed assumptions, an empty feasible set and exhausted refinement retain their explicit meanings.

