### Tiles, streams and LC evaluation · `sec:nrz:lc-closing-tiles-evaluation`

**Claim (Engine tile, mask and loan surface)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-engine-tiles-masks`

LC closing requires the engine storage surface for all admitted LC shapes: packed matching masks, initialized companion coverage, safe independent loans and repairable handback, original-association maps, gathered views/compaction, reader pins and complete atomic publication. Governing obligations: (`req:nrz:tiles-streams-matrix-owner`), (`req:nrz:tiles-streams-lifecycle-evidence`), (`req:nrz:lc-grid-mask-design`), (`req:nrz:lc-stream-host-loans`).

**Claim (Masked enclosed kernels for LC)** · `claim:nrz:lc-closing-engine-kernels`

LC closing requires the enclosed algebraic and pi-affine kernel laws used by its admitted graphs, complete total/numerical-only companions, masks and original-origin correspondence. Separately admitted trigonometric expressions do not expand the trajectory or general-argument exclusions. Governing obligations: (`req:nrz:tiles-streams-matrix-owner`), (`req:nrz:lc-evaluation-kernel-interface`), (`req:nrz:lc-evaluation-kernel-domains`), (`req:nrz:lc-evaluation-kernel-evidence`), (`req:nrz:lc-evaluation-matrix-owner`).

