LC closing requires open-axis standing answers, local thresholds, fixed-window and observed-domain decisions, complete atomic masked publication and original association. Shared-source narrowing, changed assumptions, late/corrected input and retained historical consumers preserve their distinct semantics and ordered quantifiers. Governing obligations: (`sec:nrz:lc-stream-answers`), (`sec:nrz:lc-stream-acceptance`), (`req:nrz:lc-stream-standing-bindings`), (`req:nrz:lc-stream-source-refinement`), (`sec:nrz:lc-evaluation-stream-nodes`), (`req:nrz:lc-evaluation-plan-owner`).

