LC closing requires bounded live heap, descriptor, cache and walk owners for finite and open axes; safe concurrent loans and older readers; resolvable historical evidence; and each LC node's fixed/observed-domain absence law. Completed full flush empties all numerical occupations while exact caches stay warm; partial flush preserves outside dependencies. Governing obligations: (`req:nrz:lc-grid-bounded-execution`), (`req:nrz:lc-stream-bounded-execution`), (`req:nrz:lc-evaluation-lifecycle-evidence`), (`rule:nrz:lc-stream-retirement`), (`rule:nrz:lc-stream-flush`), (`tab:nrz:lc-evaluation-flush-map`).

