LC closing requires a labelled per-cell overhead budget against (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-naive-model`), predicting each component's factor and reason without double counting. Identify carrying error radius with each value; enclosing each rounding with a priori bounds or error-free transformations, never rounding-mode switching; cycle-membership and decision comparisons against tile-level π evidence; the mask bit; writing centre and radius instead of one value; and exact tile work amortized over its actual cells. State the composition and expected total of about 4–8 times the model, including tile size, branch/sample extents, precision, setup and cache assumptions. Any additional cost has its own labelled component rather than disappearing into the total. The conceptual inventory and conditional envelope are (`sec:nrz:lc-compute-certification`), (`pred:nrz:lc-compute-overhead-envelope`); the remaining composition, attribution and observation questions are (`sec:nrz:lc-compute-open`). Governing contracts: (`rule:nrz:lc-grid-fast-path`), (`req:nrz:lc-grid-phase-receipts`), (`req:nrz:lc-grid-construction-events`), (`rule:nrz:lc-grid-ratio-information`).

