**Decision (Representation and replay are settled boundaries)** · `dec:nrz:lc-resonance-binding-settled`

Cross-process or cross-machine reruns within the supported platform (`dec:vision:supported-platform`) mean agreement within tracked error under admitted arithmetic models, with build and environment provenance; identical bits and a canonical numerical snapshot are not first-slice requirements (`prin:nrz:descriptor-binding-reproducibility`). A public Complex value is an exact descriptor symbol with an explicit optional representation (`prin:nrz:descriptor-binding-optional-values`). Every float entry is covered by at least one binding, and several symbols may read overlapping selections only with exact map proofs; matrix owns allocation lifetime independently of meaning (`prin:nrz:descriptor-binding-total`), (`rule:nrz:descriptor-binding-checked-overlap`). Results and components acquire all planned bindings before execution and publish together (`rule:nrz:descriptor-binding-result-symbols`). Typed degrees and turns are ordinary descriptors with exact checked pi scales and an admitted native affine numerical conversion. Shape-owned pi references export certified scalar normalization/restoration maps with retained definition identity, deterministic errors and both covariance axes. Live pi coordinate certificates authenticate both original normalization/restoration graph nodes, retain the exact references and share both coefficient arrays and one pi region across compatible consumers. Every consumer revalidates its original values, companions and ordered covariance targets. Direct typed unit coefficients retain the same exact/numerical separation. General quantity expressions, certified mixed norms, structural recipe execution and indexed grid admission remain with the LC-quantities step (`step:nrz:lc-resonance-quantity-bite`); complete driven/decision invariant scheduling remains with LC plans (`step:nrz:lc-resonance-physics-bite`). These representation and replay decisions do not establish complete LC delivery; standing remains in (`sec:nrz:lc-closing-register`).

**Decision (First-deliverable gates and capability cadence)** · `dec:nrz:lc-resonance-delivery-contract`

The first deliverable has no additional target-environment, latency or memory-envelope gate beyond recording the environment and measured provenance. Each execution still needs its admitted arithmetic model, numerical bounds and resource refusals. LC closing additionally requires known, explained and bounded certification cost under (`sec:nrz:lc-closing-certification-cost`): the theoretical optimized naive model, predicted overhead budget, measured component tracking and measured about-tenfold-or-less bound are closing claims. This relative-cost requirement does not impose an absolute latency or memory target, prescribe a deployment environment, or waive correctness.

