The decisions selecting LC, exact pi measures and expressions, checked float-block phasors, the restricted spectrum, graph-backed mixed meanings and explicit domain outcomes are settled design boundaries. Those decisions do not assert delivery: (`sec:nrz:lc-closing-register`) alone records implementation standing and (`rule:nrz:lc-closing-completion`) decides closure. Future trajectory APIs, broader numerical constant expressions, general Complex operations and additional deployment/performance commitments need their own capability scope; implementation choices such as a reference-selection heuristic must satisfy the explicit contracts already given. Completion requires every closing claim in (`sec:nrz:lc-closing-register`), including tile and stream execution, the LC evaluation design, cache/lambda reuse, generic nonsquare roots, independent oracle/mutation/resource/relation/reproducibility evidence and the recorded scale measurement. The actual billion-cell measurement and explained relative-cost bound must pass, and the final independent review must report `LC DONE` under (`rule:nrz:lc-closing-independent-review`). The implemented subsets and their existing evidence are recorded in (`tab:nrz:lc-resonance-capability-routes`); the remaining adapters are not implied by those successes (`rule:vision:completion-boundaries`).

